    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Parses an output color specification.</para><para>This parser is used by <ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1_1CommandLine" kindref="compound">Sawyer::CommandLine</ref> when parsing command-line switches. For instance, many ROSE tools have a &quot;--color&quot; switch. The canonical documentation for this parser comes from its <ref refid="classRose_1_1Color_1_1ColorizationParser_1a4c2be6c899030a7d05416f5d80c69bb1" kindref="member">docString</ref> function. In short, it parses one or two words separated by a comma, the words being when to use colorized output (&quot;off&quot;, &quot;on&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;) and the basic theme (&quot;dark&quot;, or &quot;light&quot;). </para>    </detaileddescription>
